      "is_best": true,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><blockquote><p> I <a href=\"https://community.st.com/feedback-forum-118/allow-to-edit-posts-166661\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow ugc\" target=\"_self\">can’t edit</a> original post</p></blockquote><p>You should have 60 minutes to edit your post:</p><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/feedback-forum-118/how-can-i-edit-my-post-after-submitting-there-s-no-edit-option-anymore-166559\"></oembed><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/feedback-forum-118/where-is-the-edit-button-166705\"></oembed><p> </p><blockquote><p>so I should add comment when I have new information/solution for a problem. </p></blockquote><p>That’s generally the best way to proceed anyhow - even if the forum did allow edits.</p><p>It causes confusion to edit an existing post - especially when people have already replied to it.</p><p> </p><blockquote><p>I suggest to not notify user about his comments.</p></blockquote><p>I agree that it’s pointless (and possibly annoying) to notify a user about <em>their own</em> activity:</p><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/feedback-forum-118/unnecessary-notifications-166172\"></oembed><p> </p></div>"
